NNAAMMEE
     oowwcc — Dallas Semiconductor 1-Wire Controller

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ddeevviiccee oowwcc

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The oowwcc module implements Dallas Semiconductor 1-Wire signaling.  It at‐
     taches the ow(4) driver 1-Wire bus protocol.  The oowwcc device implements
     the Link Layer of the 1-Wire bus protocol stack.

     Bit banging a pin on a gpiobus(4) is the only supported controller.  Both
     standard and overdrive transfer timings are implemented.  Strong pull-up
     functionality needed to support parasitic mode is not implemented.

     To enable 1-Wire for FDT systems requires modifying the DTS for your
     board to add something like:

     / {
             ...
             onewire {
                     compatible = "w1-gpio";
                     gpios = <&gpio 4 1>;
             };
             ...
     };

     The gpios property describes the GPIO pin the 1-Wire bus is connected to.
     For more details about the _g_p_i_o_s property, please consult
     _/_u_s_r_/_s_r_c_/_s_y_s_/_d_t_s_/_b_i_n_d_i_n_g_s_-_g_p_i_o_._t_x_t.

     On a device.hints(5) based system these values are required for the oowwcc:

     _h_i_n_t_._o_w_c_._%_d_._a_t     The ggppiioobbuuss you are attaching to.

     _h_i_n_t_._o_w_c_._%_d_._p_i_n_s   This is a bitmask that defines a pin on the ggppiioobbuuss
                        that is to be used for the 1-Wire bus.  For instance,
                        to configure pin 10, use the bitmask of 0x400.  Please
                        note that this mask should have only one bit set (any
                        other bits - i.e., pins - will be ignored).

